meta {
  name: Get My BeaconU Card
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/beaconu-card
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Returns the student's BeaconU card (card number, holder name, validity,
  wallet balance, total earned/withdrawn, status), plus enrollment context:

  - college_id / college_name / course_name: from the student's active
    admissions Enrollment, null if not currently enrolled anywhere.
  - duration: the enrolled course's duration + 1 year (e.g. course
    duration "3 Years" -> "4 Years"), null if not enrolled or the
    course's duration field couldn't be parsed.
  - commute_enrolled: true if the student has an active CommuteEnrollment.
  - housing_enrolled: true if the student has an active HostelEnrollment.

  The card itself is auto-issued the first time a student is enrolled at
  any college (college-admin "Mark Enrolled" action) — one card per
  student, reused across every subsequent enrollment.

  Self-healing: if the student doesn't have a card yet for any reason
  (e.g. not enrolled anywhere), calling this endpoint creates one on the
  spot instead of 404ing — every student is guaranteed a card once they
  call this. The enrollment-context fields above are computed fresh on
  every call regardless of when the card itself was issued.
}
